    {
      "type": "listeningComp",
      "audioUrl": "/audio/unit-25/testimonio-rogelio.mp3",
      "transcript": "Mira, asere, yo estaba cansadísimo. Grabé la última toma a las dos y guardé el disco. A las dos y media vino y me lo pidió. Le dije que no. A las tres volvió y me lo pidió otra vez. Y se lo di. Se lo di porque quería irme a mi casa. Me prometió que me lo devolvía por la mañana. Nunca me lo devolvió. Y yo se lo conté a todo el mundo.",
      "translation": "Look, my friend, I was exhausted. I recorded the last take at two and put the disc away. At two thirty he came and asked me for it. I said no. At three he came back and asked me for it again. And I gave it to him. I gave it to him because I wanted to go home. He promised me he would return it in the morning. He never returned it. And I told everyone about it.",
